  "status": "verified-sample",
  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 18 actions (updateActions) and 12 boolean feedbacks (initFeedbacks) in index.js. A further action, grid_display (GridDisplay), is commented out in the source (index.js, marked TODO: untested with the upgrade kit) and is therefore not registered and not catalogued.",
    "Protocol: Panasonic NTCONTROL over TCP through the npm package ntcontrol-connection (^0.5.0, lock file 0.5.0). Config default port 1024, default user and password come from the module config (index.js getConfigFields); the catalog stores no credentials. Config dropdown \"Use Feedback\" (yes/no, default yes) controls monitoring of brightness, test pattern, color matching, picture mode and operating mode.",
    "Dropdown choice lists (input, color matching, shutter fade, test pattern, lamp state, lens memory, picture mode, operating mode, focus speed) are built from enums in ntcontrol-connection 0.5.0 (dist/Types.js, read from the published npm tarball, not executed). The choice ids are the enum values as strings (for example input HDMI1 = 'HD1', lens memory 1 = '+00000'); the labels are the enum keys. A different version of the library could change these lists.",
    "Odd defaults kept as in the source: the input action and the input feedback default to '' (an id that is not in the choice list); the on/off/toggle choice ids are the strings on, off, toggle with the same text as labels.",
    "The color actions and feedbacks (color_matching_3c, color_matching_7c) take free text \"R,G,B\" triples (defaults such as 2048,0,0; the source passes them to ntcontrol DefaultRgbConverter.parse). The textinput regex is written Regex.SOMETHING in the source; its resolved value was not checked because @companion-module/base is not installed in the clone.",
    "Feedback matching: input, test_pattern, picture_mode, color_matching and operating_mode compare against the module's variables; color_matching_3c and _7c additionally require the current color matching mode, and compare the R,G,B strings for equality.",
    "Base library 1.x: options do not support expressions. Variables and presets are not catalogued."
